 "▼ Dive in: <0>Worked update</0>": "",
 "Training loop: forward pass → loss → <0>backward pass</0> (chain rule gives ∂loss/∂every weight) → small step downhill.": "",
 "For softmax + cross-entropy the gradient at the logits is beautifully simple: <0>p − y</0> (prediction minus one-hot target).": "",
 "The <0>learning rate</0> is the step size: too small crawls, too large overshoots and diverges.": "",
 "<0>AdamW</0> adapts the step per weight using running averages of gradients and squared gradients, plus decoupled weight decay.": "",
 "Backward costs ≈ {#}× the forward FLOPs, so a training step ≈ {#}× a forward pass (hence ≈ {#}·N FLOPs per token).": "",
 "Real runs use a warm-up then a decaying schedule (e.g. cosine) and gradient clipping; peak LRs for ~8B models are often around {#}⁻⁴ (hedged).": "",
 "AdamW keeps {#} extra floats per parameter (m and v) — a big part of training memory.": "",
