 "SFT = the same next-token training, but on example <0>conversations</0> written or curated to show ideal assistant behaviour.": "",
 "Conversations are flattened with a <0>chat template</0> into one token sequence.": "",
 "A <0>loss mask</0> keeps only assistant tokens in the loss: the model learns to <1>answer</1>, not to imitate users.": "",
 "Masked positions are often given label {#}, which PyTorch’s cross-entropy ignores by default (ignore_index).": "",
 "Including the end-of-turn token in the loss teaches the model when to stop.": "",
