 "▼ Dive in: <0>Reward model</0>": "",
 "Humans (or an AI judge) compare two answers to the same prompt: <0>chosen</0> vs <1>rejected</1>.": "",
 "<0>RLHF</0>: train a <1>reward model</1> on those comparisons, then optimise the policy with RL (classically PPO) to get high reward without drifting too far (KL penalty).": "",
 "<0>DPO</0> skips the reward model and RL loop: a simple classification-style loss directly on the preference pairs.": "",
 "<0>RLAIF</0> / constitutional approaches use an AI model, guided by written principles, to produce the preference labels.": "",
 "Reward model loss (Bradley–Terry): −ln σ(r_chosen − r_rejected).": "",
 "DPO loss: −ln σ(β·[(log π/π_ref)(chosen) − (log π/π_ref)(rejected)]).": "",
 "Failure mode: <0>reward hacking</0> — exploiting reward-model quirks (e.g. verbosity). The KL term and data quality mitigate it.": "",
 "preference pair": "",
 "reward r": "",
 "P(chosen ≻ rejected)": "",
