 "reward model": "",
 "Prompt: <0>“Explain why the sky is blue.”</0> The reward model <1/> scores each answer <2/> <3/>. Bradley–Terry turns the score gap into a preference probability.": "",
 "r(chosen)": "",
 "r(rejected)": "",
 "P(chosen ≻ rejected) = σ(r_c − r_r) = σ({#}) = <0>{#}</0> loss = −ln P = <1>{#}</1>": "",
 "Agrees with the human label; training still pushes the gap wider (gradient ∝ {#} − P = {#}).": "",
 "PPO objective (sketch): maximise E[ r(x, y) ] − β · KL(π ‖ π_SFT)": "",
 "The KL penalty keeps the policy close to the SFT model so it can’t drift into weird text that merely fools the reward model.": "",
