 "▼ Dive in: <0>RLAIF & caveats</0>": "",
 "RLAIF / Constitutional AI": "",
 "An AI model critiques or compares answers using a written list of principles; its judgements replace (some) human labels. Cheaper and more consistent at scale; quality depends on the judge and the principles.": "",
 "Reward hacking": "",
 "Policies tend to find what the reward model over-rewards — e.g. longer answers, confident tone, flattery. Mitigations: KL penalty, better RM data, length control, held-out human eval.": "",
 "PPO vs DPO in practice": "",
 "PPO needs {#} models in memory (policy, reference, reward, value) and is finicky; DPO needs {#} and is stable. Many recipes combine methods; the trade-offs are still debated.": "",
 "These methods change <0>which</0> plausible answer is preferred much more than they add knowledge. Research suggests most capabilities come from pretraining.": "",
