 "h = W·x + (α/r)·B·(A·x) — only A and B get gradients.": "",
 "Intuition: the change needed to adapt a model to a task is (empirically) low-rank — a few directions matter. LoRA bets on that.": "",
 "▼ Dive in: <0>Rank slider</0>": "",
 "Freeze the big weight W. Learn a small update <0>ΔW = B·A</0> with rank r ≪ d. Effective weight: <1>W + (α/r)·B·A</1>.": "",
 "For a {#} × {#} projection, r = {#} trains {#}·{#}·{#} = {#} numbers instead of {#} M.": "",
 "Adapters are a few MB to a few hundred MB — swap them per task on one shared base model.": "",
 "B is initialised to zero, so training starts exactly at the base model.": "",
 "After training, B·A can be merged into W: zero extra inference latency.": "",
 "QLoRA keeps the frozen base in {#}-bit to save even more memory (see <0>LoRA tracking</0>).": "",
